        ('scripture', 'Mark 16:20', 'And they went out and preached everywhere, the Lord working with them and confirming the word through the accompanying signs. Amen.'),
        ('h3', 'Demonstration, not persuasion'),
        ('p', 'The apostles’ ministry pattern was never rhetorical polish; it was demonstration of the Spirit and of power, so that faith would rest on God, not on human eloquence.'),
        ('scripture', '1 Corinthians 2:4', 'And my speech and my preaching were not with persuasive words of human wisdom, but in demonstration of the Spirit and of power.'),
        ('callout', 'depth', 'Wommack’s phrase "like ringing the dinner bell" captures a central caution: a miracle is meant to draw people to the meal, the Gospel itself, not to become the meal. A ministry that chases signs for their own sake has mistaken the invitation for the feast.'),
